## NOTE (defect INT-D11): each store's own fingerprint config_sha256 covers only: ['corpus-rules.yaml', 'pinned-view.yaml'] -- with a view outside config/, _config_sha256 hashes the VIEW's directory, so config/{embed-profile,id-grammar,authority-registry,model-pin,state-aliases}.yaml, which the layer builders read, are not fingerprinted
## the converse, measured after this audit wrote EVIDENCE/repair-1/INT-VERDICT.yaml beside the pinned view (independent dry-run, no build):
#   compute_fingerprint + determine_trigger on store-b -> ('FULL', []) with config_sha256 keys ['INT-VERDICT.yaml', 'corpus-rules.yaml',
#   'pinned-view.yaml'] -- an unrelated file in the view's directory forces a full rebuild (INT-D11). All NOOP checks above ran before it existed.
